false,[78,79],"dimensions","3D","World models","Development stages",[83,84,79],"stages","Gameplay & code","Testing","Topics",[88,89,90,91,92],"tags","code-world-model","executable-state","hybrid-renderer","persistent-state","CombatStateBench","Further reading",[95],{"_52":96,"_25":97},"Project and release progress","https://github.com/AlayaLab/pwm","Project source",[100],{"_52":98,"_25":101},"https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.10540","Why it belongs here","An agent converts instructions into entity states and state-transition programs. A lightweight engine maintains global state, then compiles stateful 3D oriented bounding boxes and camera trajectories into video model controls. The paper introduces CombatStateBench to check entity counts and irreversible states. The public repository currently centers on project documentation, which does not establish that complete inference code and weights are available.","detail","guidance","Resource type","Paper","Category","category","lead","summary","name","world","paper",[123],[88,89,90,91,92],[121,122,113],[120,113],2026,"3d","code","test",{"_52":96,"_25":97},{"_125":126},"documents",{"_127":128,"_129":130},"en",[132,136,137,138,135,139,140,141,142,143,144,145,146,147,148,149,150,151,152,153,154,155,156,157,158,159,160,161,162,163,164,165,166,167,168,169,170,134,171,133,172,173,174,175,176,177,178,179,180,181,182,183,184,185,186,187,188,189],"zh",[131,132,133,134,135],"reading-guide","practical-guide","level-design-skill","deployment","publishing-platforms","tutorials-and-demos","coding-agent-game-code","game-testing-library","agents-notes","engines-notes","game-ai-notes","cadle-repositories","world-model-notes","research-index","production-research-notes","engine-operation-contracts","production-work-orders","studio-production-case-studies","native-operation-details","production-debugging-contracts","production-coverage-gaps","generative-tools-research","generative-api-boundaries","generation-delivery-contracts","asset-validation-